{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Upavāṇa","html":"<article id='thag2.33'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 2.33 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 2.33 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Catutthavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Four </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Upavāṇattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Upavāṇa </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Arahaṁ sugato loke, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The perfected one, the Holy One in the world, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vātehābādhiko muni; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the sage is afflicted by winds. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sace uṇhodakaṁ atthi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>If there’s hot water, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>munino dehi brāhmaṇa. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>give it to the sage, brahmin. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pūjito pūjaneyyānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I wish to bring it to the one </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sakkareyyāna sakkato; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who is esteemed by the estimable, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Apacitopaceyyānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>honored by the honorable, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tassa icchāmi hātave”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and venerated by the venerable. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Upavāṇo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
